            <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 font-medium">Feb 2</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Health care and early childhood education (FW, IS)</td><td class="px-3 py-2">1,649</td><td class="px-3 py-2">FW 36, IS 56</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 font-medium">Feb 2</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Physicians (FW)</td><td class="px-3 py-2">129</td><td class="px-3 py-2">33</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="px-3 py-2 font-medium">Feb 2</td><td class="px-3 py-2">REDI pilot (FW, IS, IDS)</td><td class="px-3 py-2">47</td><td class="px-3 py-2">FW 44, IS 69, IDS 34</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        By our count, these rounds add up to 13,642 invitations between February 2 and April 30, 2026. Invitations are not nominations: some invited candidates do not apply, and some applications are refused. Three patterns stand out. Health care and early childhood education rounds had by far the lowest Foreign Worker cutoffs (20 in April). International Student cutoffs were consistently the highest, often in the 80s. And regional rounds outside the GTA were held often, which fits the new OWP scoring that rewards jobs outside Toronto.
      </p>
      <p>
        People still search for "OINP draw 2025" to compare. Because every 2025 round was held under streams that no longer exist, those cutoffs tell you little about your chances in the OWP stream.
      </p>

      <h2 id="fees" class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Fees, Deadlines and Processing</h2>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
        <li><strong>EOI registration:</strong> free.</li>
        <li><strong>OWP application fee:</strong> $1,500 if the job (or a physician's practice) is outside the GTA; $2,000 in the City of Toronto, Durham, Halton, Peel or York. Payment is by Visa or Mastercard (credit or debit) only. The fee is refunded only if the application is incomplete or withdrawn before processing starts.</li>
        <li><strong>After an invitation:</strong> your employer has 14 calendar days to submit its part, and you have 17 calendar days to submit your application and pay, after your employer has filed.</li>
        <li><strong>After nomination:</strong> six months to apply to IRCC. For an Express Entry enhanced nomination you have 30 days to accept it and 60 days after accepting to submit to IRCC.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The OINP pages we checked on November 13, 2026 do not publish a processing time for OWP applications, and none had been processed under a published draw by that date. IRCC's permanent residence processing comes on top of the provincial stage and is shown on IRCC's processing-time tool.
      </p>

      <h2 id="bc" class="text-3xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Ontario PNP vs BC PNP in Late 2026</h2>

      <p>
        Ontario and British Columbia have moved in the same direction this year: fewer open doors and more weight on employers and priority occupations. B.C. closed its student and graduate streams, and since April 23, 2026 it invites mainly in three priorities: Care (health, childcare, education and veterinary occupations), Build (certified trades) and Innovate (high economic impact candidates). Its Skills Immigration streams need a job offer from an eligible B.C. employer, much like Ontario's OWP.
      </p>

