          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        If you already work in one province, that province is usually your strongest option, because both programs reward experience with the employer making the offer. For a fuller side-by-side, read <a href="/articles/bc-pnp-vs-ontario-oinp-2026" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">BC PNP vs Ontario OINP 2026</a>. To see how your profile would score in B.C., use the <a href="/bc-pnp-calculator" class="text-indigo-600 underline font-semibold">BC PNP Calculator</a> and compare it with recent <a href="/bc-pnp-draws" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">BC PNP draws</a>. For other provinces, see our <a href="/articles/canada-pnp-news-2026-all-provinces" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">2026 PNP news across all provinces</a> and <a href="/articles/best-provinces-pnp-2027" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline">best provinces for a PNP in 2027</a>.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">What to do now if you are aiming for Ontario</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
        <li>Confirm your employer meets the OWP employer rules (three years in business, Ontario premises, revenue and staffing thresholds) before it submits the job offer.</li>
        <li>Register your EOI within 30 days of the employer's submission, and keep your language test less than two years old.</li>
        <li>If you earned $80,000 or more in one year in the last five, make sure a CRA Notice of Assessment backs it up. The 10 points apply automatically.</li>
        <li>Watch the official updates page rather than social media for the first OWP round. Avoid anyone selling "guaranteed" Ontario job offers: the November 9 list of penalized employers and representatives shows the OINP is enforcing its rules.</li>
      </ul>

